# Gate 4 whitelist — names with no production reference YET.
#
# Two rules, both enforced by tests:
#   1. Every entry needs a reason after the '#'.
#   2. Any entry deferring to future wiring must name the TASK that wires it,
#      and the gate FAILS once that task is marked complete. The list therefore
#      shrinks by construction as phases close. An entry that outlives its task
#      announces itself instead of becoming permanent furniture.
#
# Entries here are DEBT. An entry justified without deferral (an ops read
# surface, say) needs no task, because it is not waiting on anything.

# --- wired by the US1 evaluation loop (T056) ---------------------------------
evaluate_all      # the supervised loop is driven by T056
compute           # fingerprint identity, consulted per evaluation in T056
release           # all three entry conditions call it; first one lands T056
record            # AuditLog.record, called from the release path in T056
thread_for        # resolves the rule's thread before injection in T056
inject            # the injection itself, T056
configure_tools   # thread tools set before injection, T056
poll              # CompletionSource; the loop is source-agnostic, T056
forget            # called when a recorded thread 404s, T056

# --- wired by the US2 scheduler loop (T061) ----------------------------------
next_wakeup       # the sleep-until-due timer, T061
mark_fired        # records a served instant, T061
prune             # scheduler retention sweep, T061
maybe_reset       # fingerprint daily reset, driven by the same sweep, T061
known_rules       # enumerated by the retention sweep, T061

# --- wired by US3 coalescing (T065) ------------------------------------------
is_due            # CoalesceWindow, the window timer, T065
drain             # CoalesceWindow, flushes on close, T065

# --- wired by US4 presence-aware routing (T068) ------------------------------
observe_runs      # presence updated from run records before routing, T068

# --- ops read surfaces: not deferred, so no task -----------------------------
describe          # runtime inspection of presence (FR-023); read by operators
entries           # audit log read side; read by operators and by tests
count             # fingerprint store size; read by operators and by tests
